From 10a21dc51a5b1316480206733b62a9ddbec60b9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abayoumy <abayoumy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:16:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Protection: per-channel current and power limits (settings
 v8)

Add opt-in per-channel overcurrent and overpower limits alongside the
existing aggregate temperature/current/power limits. Enable bits 0..2 keep
their shipped v4..v7 meaning; bits 3..4 are new, so stored records, the
/api/config projection and the existing MQTT contract are unchanged.

The settings body moves to version 8 with the per-channel limits appended
after the timers: every v4..v7 reader stays intact, and a record already in
flash still loads with the per-channel limits left at their defaults.

Two defects found while redoing the earlier attempt, both silent on device:
- power limits are stored in W while samples arrive in mW, so the limit has
  to be scaled before comparing; the first attempt tripped at 1/1000 of the
  configured load;
- the per-channel confirmation counters must be cleared together with the
  aggregate ones, including after a temperature trip.

The redo also keeps the aggregate limits as separate judgements and drops
the unused scalar-to-array conversion of protection.current_ma/power_w that
made the first attempt fail to compile.

Adds source/standalone/host_test: a host-cc test (no cross toolchain) that
covers the trip logic, the W/mW boundary, settings v8 round-trip, the
rejection paths and the v4..v7 -> v8 migration of a record already stored on
a device. It caught an interleaved-array codec bug during development.
